  * SWEET: USB bring-up, step 1 - read-only state probe.
  *
  * The phone's USB is a Synopsys DWC3 (USB 2.0 only, maximum-speed
- * high-speed) at 0x0a600000 behind Qualcomm's dwc-usb3-msm wrapper, with a
- * QUSB2 PHY at 0x088e2000; its power domain is the USB30_PRIM GDSC and its
- * clocks come from GCC (offsets from Linux gcc-sdmmagpie.c). ABL uses this
- * controller for fastboot; this probe only reports what state it is left
- * in after `fastboot boot`. It never writes a register, and it touches the
- * DWC3 / PHY register blocks only when the GCC status registers say their
- * power domain and clocks are on (an access to a gated block would hang).
+ * high-speed) at 0x0a600000 behind Qualcomm's dwc-usb3-msm wrapper, with an
+ * eUSB2 PHY at 0x088e3000; its power domain is the USB30_PRIM GDSC and its
+ * clocks come from GCC (offsets from the downstream gcc-cliffs.c driver).
+ * The wrapper register file is inside the DWC3 core_base window on this SoC
+ * (dwc3-qcom.c ioremaps reg[0] as "qscratch"), unlike sweet's separate
+ * 0xa6f8800 block. ABL uses this controller for fastboot; this probe only
+ * reports what state it is left in after `fastboot boot`. It never writes a
+ * register, and it touches the DWC3 / PHY register blocks only when the GCC
+ * status registers say their power domain and clocks are on (an access to a
+ * gated block would hang).
  */
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
 #include <sys/param.h>
@@ -43,27 +46,27 @@
 extern ppnum_t pmap_find_phys(pmap_t pmap, addr64_t va);
 
